The LLM-built exploits covered non-PIE builds only, first without ASLR and then with ASLR; against the default PIE build the working exploit came from the human researcher by way of a stack leak, which the LLM never reached ([XBOW, 2026-05-12](https://xbow.com/blog/dead-letter-cve-2026-45185-xbow-found-rce-exim)). The Exim maintainers state there is no known mitigation other than upgrading, so suppressing the CHUNKING advertisement is not a vendor-endorsed workaround, and their advisory, not XBOW's post, sets the CVSS 9.8 and the affected range of 4.97 up to and including 4.99.2 on builds using GnuTLS, fixed in 4.99.3 ([Exim advisory, 2026-05-12](https://exim.org/static/doc/security/EXIM-Security-2026-05-01.1/EXIM-Security-2026-05-01.1.txt)). Exposure further requires STARTTLS and CHUNKING to be advertised ([oss-security, 2026-05-12](https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/05/12/4)).
